CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $881,068 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $447K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 34%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $1K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Evolent Health, Inc is a small-cap healthcare business with a $518M market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +34% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $5M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 0 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -30.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -7.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.4) \u2014 the kind